#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""vpn-relay-agent — the only thing the main server's bot may run on a relay (docs/relay.md).

The relay has no Telegram bot and never talks to the Telegram API. The bot on the main
server manages it over SSH with ONE key, whose line in root's authorized_keys is

    restrict,command="/usr/local/sbin/vpn-relay-agent" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... vpn-relay-agent

so whatever the client asks for, sshd runs this program, with the request in
SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND. Nothing of it reaches a shell. The request must match one line
of the whitelist EXACTLY (full-string regular expressions, length-capped, ASCII only);
everything else is refused with exit 2 before anything is read or changed:

    hello <token>                         complete the pairing (43-char base64url token)
    status                                facts about the relay, read-only
    apply target=<dns name> tcp=<ports> udp=<ports>
                                          re-point / re-port the forward; rolled back
                                          when the ruleset or its check fails
    update                                deploy the newest release tag (never backwards
                                          or sideways) with scripts/deploy.sh — the
                                          relay's one update engine
    uninstall                             remove everything scripts/install.sh installed
    input-confirm                         run `vpn-relay-apply input-confirm` from THIS
                                          ssh session (a new one: the bot's own proof
                                          that the input filter lets ssh in)
    jump key=<ed25519 blob> open=<host>:<port>[,<host>:<port>...]
                                          a hub: write the bot's ONE jump line (below)
    jump-off                              a hub: remove that line

Before a successful `hello` only `hello` is accepted. `hello` compares sha256(token)
with the hash scripts/install.sh stored from the pairing code (constant time), within
the code's expiry; a repeated `hello` with the SAME token after the pairing answers
again (the bot may retry its checks), any other token is refused.

Output: ONE JSON object on stdout — {"ok": true|false, "cmd": ..., ...}. Exit codes:
0 ok · 2 refused (not on the whitelist, a bad argument) · 3 not allowed (token, not
paired, expired) · 4 failed (the operation itself; the relay is as it was) · 5 busy
(another mutating call holds the lock).

Every call is logged to the journal (logger -t vpn-relay-agent) with the command
name, the caller's address and the verdict — never the token.

THE JUMP LINE (a hub, docs/relay.md «Управление RU-relay через hub»). In the fallback
mode the TSPU cuts SSH from the main server to the RU relays; the bot reaches them
THROUGH the hub with a second key of its own, the jump key. `jump` keeps exactly ONE
line for it in root's authorized_keys:

    restrict,port-forwarding,permitopen="<host>:<port>"[,permitopen="..."],command="/bin/false" ssh-ed25519 <blob> vpn-bot-relay-jump

restrict (no pty, no agent/X11 forwarding, no user rc) + port-forwarding back, but only
to the listed relays' sshd (permitopen — sshd compares the host character for character,
so hosts are lower-cased here and the bot's -W is too), and /bin/false for any session:
no shell. The values are
validated here (DNS name or IPv4, port 1..65535, at most 32, unique); a key that already
has another line in the file (the agent's own key among them) is refused. And `jump` is
refused until `sshd -T` shows forwarding LOCAL TCP only (allowtcpforwarding local,
allowstreamlocalforwarding no): port-forwarding in the key would otherwise also let
it open listeners here (ssh -R: TCP ports, root-owned Unix sockets), which no
authorized_keys option forbids. scripts/deploy.sh installs that setting on every relay
(deploy/host/ssh/00-vpnrelay-forwarding.conf). Every other
line of the file stays byte-identical: the old jump line is replaced where it stands,
or the new one appended. `jump-off` removes it; `uninstall` too.

`input-confirm` runs the helper as a direct child, so the ssh session the bot opened is
among its ancestors — the check «the session began after the filter was applied» is
the proof. It does not take the agent's lock: the filter waits for its confirmation
exactly while `update` (the deploy that applied it) holds that lock.

`update` and `uninstall` run in a transient systemd unit (systemd-run --wait), so a
dropped SSH connection cannot cut them in half. Their bodies are the internal entry
points `--internal-update` / `--internal-uninstall`, which only root can start and
which refuse to run inside an SSH session: the SSH client cannot reach them (a
forced command gets no argv).

`update` does not install anything itself. It picks the newest release tag (the rule
scripts/deploy.sh's relay_latest_release carries too — tests/test_relay_release_tag.py
runs both on the same tags), refuses to go backwards or sideways, and hands the move to
the deploy an operator runs by hand: scripts/redeploy.sh with DEPLOY_REF=<tag>
(deploy.sh of that tag, in its own transient unit, its log under /root). deploy.sh
gates, installs the helpers, units and host files, verifies and rolls back by itself;
the result lands in /var/lib/vpn-relay/update.json.

TEST SEAM: VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST=1 (ignored inside an SSH session) re-roots every
path under VPN_RELAY_AGENT_ROOT and runs external commands only from
VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST_BIN. sshd passes no such variable (AcceptEnv is LANG LC_*
at most, PermitUserEnvironment is off), and the seam is off whenever SSH_CONNECTION
is set.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import base64
import binascii
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import hmac
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess  # noqa: S404 — fixed argv lists of system tools, never a shell
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from collections.abc import Iterator, Sequence
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

# 2: input-confirm, jump, jump-off; input_status and jump in the facts. The protocol
# (what `hello` answers) is unchanged.
AGENT_VERSION = "2"
PROTOCOL = 1
# A `jump` list is the longest request (up to 32 host:port entries).
MAX_REQUEST = 4096
MAX_JUMP_OPEN = 32
# Accepted `hello` after the code's expiry (clock skew between the two hosts).
HELLO_GRACE_SECONDS = 900
MAX_PORTS = 8

SELFTEST = os.environ.get("VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST") == "1" and "SSH_CONNECTION" not in os.environ
_ROOT = os.environ.get("VPN_RELAY_AGENT_ROOT", "") if SELFTEST else ""
_BIN = os.environ.get("VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST_BIN", "") if SELFTEST else ""


def P(path: str) -> Path:
    """A host path, re-rooted under the test seam."""
    return Path(_ROOT + path) if _ROOT else Path(path)


APP_DIR = P("/opt/vpn-service")
ENV_FILE = P("/opt/vpn-service/.env")
STATE_DIR = P("/etc/vpn-relay")
PAIRING_FILE = P("/etc/vpn-relay/pairing.json")
INSTALL_FILE = P("/etc/vpn-relay/install.json")
UPSTREAM_STATE = P("/etc/vpn-relay/upstream.resolved")
VAR_DIR = P("/var/lib/vpn-relay")
UPDATE_FILE = P("/var/lib/vpn-relay/update.json")
LOCK_FILE = P("/run/vpn-relay-agent.lock")
# authorized_keys has its own lock: a hub's `update` holds LOCK_FILE for minutes and the
# jump list must still follow the relays behind it.
JUMP_LOCK_FILE = P("/run/vpn-relay-agent.jump.lock")
DEFAULT_AUTHORIZED_KEYS = "/root/.ssh/authorized_keys"
UNINSTALL_RESULT = P("/run/vpn-relay-uninstall.json")
APPLY_HELPER = "/usr/local/sbin/vpn-relay-apply"
AGENT_PATH = "/usr/local/sbin/vpn-relay-agent"
UNIT_DIR = P("/etc/systemd/system")
SYSCTL_FILE = P("/etc/sysctl.d/90-vpn-relay.conf")
# The relay's units come from the checkout (relay_units below), never from a list here.
DATA_PLANE_UNIT = "vpn-relay.service"
# What an installed relay unit is called (only the fallback without a checkout reads it):
# vpn-relay.service and vpn-relay-<name>.service|.timer. tests/test_vpn_relay_agent.py
# pins that every unit of deploy/relay/ matches, so the fallback covers the whole set.
INSTALLED_UNIT_RE = re.compile(r"vpn-relay(?:-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*)?\.(?:service|timer)")
TABLES = (("ip", "vpnrelay"), ("inet", "vpnrelay_input"))
SAFE_PATH = "/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
# `update` runs the whole deploy (the pytest gate included) inside its transient unit;
# the bot waits this long plus a minute for the answer (services/relays.py).
UPDATE_TIMEOUT = 2700
# What redeploy.sh prints when it starts deploy.sh, and the reports deploy.sh ends with.
REDEPLOY = "scripts/redeploy.sh"
# (redeploy.sh's "launching ... (log: <path>)" line: _DV_LOG of the DEPLOY VERDICT block.)
DEPLOY_OK = "===== DEPLOY OK (relay) ====="
ROLLBACK_REPORT = "===== ROLLBACK REPORT (relay) ====="
# RELEASE TAG RULE (scripts/deploy.sh relay_latest_release is the same rule):
# vMAJOR.MINOR[.PATCH[.BUILD]] in ASCII digits; `v.3.1.0`, `v3`, `v3.1.0-rc1` are not.
RELEASE_TAG_RE = re.compile(r"v[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+){1,3}")
TAG_LIST = ("tag", "-l", "--sort=refname", "v*")
KEY_MARKER = f'command="{AGENT_PATH}"'
# The jump line: its options start with this, its comment is JUMP_COMMENT.
JUMP_PREFIX = "restrict,port-forwarding,"
JUMP_COMMENT = "vpn-bot-relay-jump"
JUMP_COMMAND = 'command="/bin/false"'

E_OK, E_REFUSED, E_DENIED, E_FAILED, E_BUSY = 0, 2, 3, 4, 5

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The whitelist. Full-string matches; nothing else is ever parsed.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
_TOKEN_RE = r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}"
_PORTS = r"[0-9]{1,5}(?:,[0-9]{1,5}){0,7}"
_HOST = r"[A-Za-z0-9.-]{1,253}"
# An ed25519 public key's base64 blob ("ssh-ed25519" + 32 bytes): always 68 characters.
_ED25519_BLOB = r"AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAI[A-Za-z0-9+/]{43}"
_OPEN = rf"{_HOST}:[0-9]{{1,5}}"
# services/relay_ssh.py _REQUEST is the same list (tests/test_relay_jump.py runs both).
WHITELIST: dict[str, re.Pattern[str]] = {
    "hello": re.compile(rf"hello (?P<token>{_TOKEN_RE})"),
    "status": re.compile(r"status"),
    "apply": re.compile(rf"apply target=(?P<target>{_HOST}) tcp=(?P<tcp>{_PORTS}) udp=(?P<udp>{_PORTS})"),
    "update": re.compile(r"update"),
    "uninstall": re.compile(r"uninstall"),
    "input-confirm": re.compile(r"input-confirm"),
    "jump": re.compile(
        rf"jump key=(?P<key>{_ED25519_BLOB}) open=(?P<open>{_OPEN}(?:,{_OPEN}){{0,{MAX_JUMP_OPEN - 1}}})"
    ),
    "jump-off": re.compile(r"jump-off"),
}
_LABEL = re.compile(r"(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)")


class Refused(Exception):
    """A request that is not on the whitelist or carries a bad argument (exit 2)."""


class Denied(Exception):
    """Not allowed: token, pairing, expiry (exit 3)."""


class Failed(Exception):
    """The operation failed; whatever it changed was put back (exit 4).

    *extra* goes into the answer next to ``error`` (``update``: the whole result, so
    the bot can show the cause, the failing step and the lines that tell it)."""

    def __init__(self, message: str, extra: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> None:
        super().__init__(message)
        self.extra = dict(extra or {})


class Busy(Exception):
    """Another mutating call holds the lock (exit 5)."""


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Validation (the bot validates the same way first: services/relay_pairing.py)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def valid_dns_name(value: str) -> bool:
    """A DNS name with at least two labels, not an IPv4 literal."""
    if not value or len(value) > 253 or value.endswith(".") or "." not in value:
        return False
    labels = value.split(".")
    if not all(_LABEL.fullmatch(label) for label in labels):
        return False
    return not labels[-1].isdigit()


def parse_ports(raw: str) -> list[int]:
    items = raw.split(",")
    if not raw or len(items) > MAX_PORTS:
        raise Refused("ports: 1..8 comma-separated ports")
    ports: list[int] = []
    for item in items:
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[1-9][0-9]{0,4}", item) or int(item) > 65535:
            raise Refused(f"ports: {item!r} is not a port in 1..65535")
        if int(item) in ports:
            raise Refused(f"ports: {item} twice")
        ports.append(int(item))
    return sorted(ports)


def valid_ipv4(value: str) -> bool:
    """A dotted-quad IPv4 that can be a relay's sshd (no loopback, 0/8, link-local,
    multicast or broadcast)."""
    parts = value.split(".")
    if len(parts) != 4 or not all(re.fullmatch(r"0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2}", p) and int(p) <= 255 for p in parts):
        return False
    first, second = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])
    return first not in (0, 127, 255) and first < 224 and not (first == 169 and second == 254)


def parse_opens(raw: str) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:
    """The relays a jump line opens: host:port entries, each host a DNS name or an
    IPv4, each port 1..65535, unique, at most MAX_JUMP_OPEN — sorted."""
    items = raw.split(",")
    if not raw or len(items) > MAX_JUMP_OPEN:
        raise Refused(f"open: 1..{MAX_JUMP_OPEN} host:port entries")
    seen: list[tuple[str, int]] = []
    for item in items:
        host, sep, port = item.rpartition(":")
        host = host.lower()
        if not sep or not (valid_dns_name(host) or valid_ipv4(host)):
            raise Refused(f"open: {item!r} is not <dns name or ipv4>:<port>")
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[1-9][0-9]{0,4}", port) or int(port) > 65535:
            raise Refused(f"open: {item!r} — the port is not in 1..65535")
        if (host, int(port)) in seen:
            raise Refused(f"open: {host}:{port} twice")
        seen.append((host, int(port)))
    return sorted(seen)


def ed25519_blob(blob: str) -> str:
    """*blob* when it decodes to an ssh-ed25519 public key (type + 32 bytes), else Refused."""
    try:
        raw = base64.b64decode(blob, validate=True)
    except (ValueError, binascii.Error):
        raise Refused("key: not base64") from None
    if len(raw) != 51 or not raw.startswith(b"\x00\x00\x00\x0bssh-ed25519\x00\x00\x00\x20"):
        raise Refused("key: not an ssh-ed25519 public key")
    return blob


def parse_request(raw: str | None) -> tuple[str, dict[str, str]]:
    """The whitelisted command and its named arguments, or Refused."""
    if raw is None:
        raise Refused("no command (this key only runs the relay agent)")
    if len(raw) > MAX_REQUEST or not raw.isascii() or not raw.isprintable():
        raise Refused("malformed request")
    for name, pattern in WHITELIST.items():
        match = pattern.fullmatch(raw)
        if match is not None:
            return name, {k: v for k, v in match.groupdict().items() if v is not None}
    raise Refused("not an agent command")


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Small host helpers
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def command_env(extra: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> dict[str, str]:
    """A fixed environment for every external command: nothing the caller sent, plus
    the fixed knobs *extra* the agent itself sets (update's DEPLOY_REF)."""
    path = f"{_BIN}:{SAFE_PATH}" if _BIN else SAFE_PATH
    env = {"PATH": path, "LC_ALL": "C", "LANG": "C", **(extra or {})}
    if SELFTEST:
        # The whole seam, or a nested agent (update/uninstall) would run on the host.
        env.update(VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST="1", VPN_RELAY_AGENT_ROOT=_ROOT, VPN_RELAY_AGENT_SELFTEST_BIN=_BIN)
    return env


def run(
    args: Sequence[str], *, timeout: float = 60, check: bool = False, env: dict[str, str] | None = None
) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    if _BIN:
        exe = Path(_BIN) / Path(args[0]).name
        if not exe.exists():
            return subprocess.CompletedProcess(list(args), 127, "", f"selftest: no stub for {args[0]}")
        args = [str(exe), *args[1:]]
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(  # noqa: S603 — argv only, fixed programs, never a shell
            list(args),
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            # A byte that is not UTF-8 in a deploy's output must not crash `update`
            # (the bot would show its stale "running" line as the error).
            errors="replace",
            timeout=timeout,
            env=command_env(env),
            check=False,
            stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
        )
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(list(args), 127, "", f"{args[0]}: not found")
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(list(args), 124, "", f"{args[0]}: timeout after {timeout}s")
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise Failed(f"{Path(args[0]).name} exit {result.returncode}: {tail(result.stderr or result.stdout)}")
    return result


def tail(text: str, lines: int = 12) -> str:
    return "\n".join(text.strip().splitlines()[-lines:])


def journal(message: str) -> None:
    with contextlib.suppress(Exception):
        run(["logger", "-t", "vpn-relay-agent", "--", message], timeout=5)


def read_json(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def write_atomic(path: Path, text: str, mode: int = 0o600) -> None:
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=path.parent, prefix=f".{path.name}.")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(text)
            fh.flush()
            os.fsync(fh.fileno())
        os.chmod(tmp, mode)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.unlink(tmp)
        raise


def write_json(path: Path, data: dict[str, Any], mode: int = 0o600) -> None:
    write_atomic(path, json.dumps(data, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n", mode)


@contextlib.contextmanager
def exclusive(lock: Path | None = None) -> Iterator[None]:
    path = LOCK_FILE if lock is None else lock
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
    try:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            raise Busy("another agent call is running") from None
        yield
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# .env (the same reader as vpn-relay-apply / deploy.sh: last assignment wins)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def _assignment(key: str) -> re.Pattern[str]:
    return re.compile(rf"^\s*(?:export\s+)?{re.escape(key)}\s*=\s*(?P<value>.*)$")


def env_value(text: str, key: str) -> str:
    value = ""
    pattern = _assignment(key)
    for line in text.splitlines():
        match = pattern.match(line)
        if match:
            value = match["value"]
    value = re.sub(r"\s*#.*$", "", value).strip()
    if len(value) >= 2 and value[0] == value[-1] and value[0] in "\"'":
        value = value[1:-1]
    return value


def env_with(text: str, values: dict[str, str | None]) -> str:
    """*text* with each key set (its last assignment replaced, others dropped) or removed (None)."""
    lines = text.splitlines()
    for key, value in values.items():
        pattern = _assignment(key)
        hits = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if pattern.match(line)]
        if value is None:
            lines = [line for i, line in enumerate(lines) if i not in hits]
            continue
        if hits:
            lines[hits[-1]] = f"{key}={value}"
            lines = [line for i, line in enumerate(lines) if i not in hits[:-1]]
        else:
            lines.append(f"{key}={value}")
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"


def read_env() -> str:
    try:
        return ENV_FILE.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Failed(f"{ENV_FILE} is unreadable: {exc}") from None


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Facts
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def ports_of(raw: str) -> list[int]:
    try:
        return parse_ports(raw.replace(" ", "")) if raw else [443]
    except Refused:
        return []


def live_target() -> str | None:
    out = run(["nft", "list", "table", "ip", "vpnrelay"], timeout=10)
    if out.returncode != 0:
        return None
    targets = sorted(set(re.findall(r"dnat to ([0-9.]+):[0-9]+", out.stdout)))
    return targets[0] if len(targets) == 1 else None


def resolve(name: str) -> list[str]:
    out = run(["getent", "ahostsv4", name], timeout=15)
    found = {line.split()[0] for line in out.stdout.splitlines() if line.split()}
    return sorted(a for a in found if re.fullmatch(r"(?:[0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}", a))


def ssh_ports() -> list[int]:
    """TCP ports sshd listens on (or systemd holds for ssh.socket)."""
    ports: set[int] = set()
    out = run(["ss", "-Hltnp"], timeout=10)
    for line in out.stdout.splitlines():
        fields = line.split()
        if len(fields) < 4 or '"sshd' not in line:
            continue
        port = fields[3].rsplit(":", 1)[-1]
        if port.isdigit():
            ports.add(int(port))
    sock = run(["systemctl", "show", "-p", "Listen", "ssh.socket"], timeout=10)
    for port in re.findall(r":([0-9]{1,5}) \(Stream\)", sock.stdout):
        ports.add(int(port))
    return sorted(ports)


def unit_state(unit: str) -> str:
    return run(["systemctl", "is-active", unit], timeout=10).stdout.strip() or "unknown"


def checkout_unit_names(checkout: Path) -> list[str]:
    """``relay_unit_names`` of scripts/deploy.sh, install.sh and vpn-bot-host-check.

    Every deploy/relay/*.service and *.timer of <checkout> (the basename), never an
    *.example.* file. It is the same rule, so a unit added to deploy/relay/ is
    stopped, disabled and removed by `uninstall` and shown by `status` as soon as
    deploy/install install it (tests/test_vpn_relay_agent.py pins the sets equal).
    Like the bash glob, a dotfile is not a match and a symlink to a file is.
    """
    src = checkout / "deploy" / "relay"
    names: list[str] = []
    for suffix in (".service", ".timer"):
        names.extend(
            path.name for path in sorted(src.glob(f"*{suffix}"))
            if not path.name.startswith(".") and ".example." not in path.name and path.is_file()
        )
    return names


def installed_unit_names() -> list[str]:
    """The relay unit files actually present in UNIT_DIR (INSTALLED_UNIT_RE)."""
    try:
        entries = sorted(UNIT_DIR.iterdir())
    except OSError:
        return []
    return [p.name for p in entries if INSTALLED_UNIT_RE.fullmatch(p.name) and p.is_file()]


def stop_order(names: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Timers first, then the oneshots they run, the data plane last.

    A timer stopped first cannot fire its oneshot (vpn-relay-apply resolve) between
    the steps; vpn-relay.service goes last because its ExecStop removes the tables,
    and nothing may re-apply them after that.
    """
    unique = sorted(set(names))
    timers = [n for n in unique if n.endswith(".timer")]
    services = [n for n in unique if n.endswith(".service") and n != DATA_PLANE_UNIT]
    return [*timers, *services, *([DATA_PLANE_UNIT] if DATA_PLANE_UNIT in unique else [])]


def relay_units() -> list[str]:
    """The relay's unit set, in stop_order; vpn-relay.service is always in it.

    From the checkout (checkout_unit_names of APP_DIR) when it carries the data plane
    — the set deploy.sh / install.sh installed from it, and nothing else.

    Without it (the checkout was removed or moved to a ref without deploy/relay/) the
    files decide: the vpn-relay*.service|.timer unit files present in UNIT_DIR, plus
    vpn-relay.service (stopping a unit whose file is gone is harmless, a running data
    plane left behind is not). Not a list frozen into the agent: that is the drift
    this function removes, and the files on the host are exactly what uninstall has
    to remove, whichever release installed them. The name pattern keeps it to the
    installer's naming, on a host installer_relay proved is a relay install.sh
    installed (the input filter's dead-man timer is transient, never in UNIT_DIR).
    """
    names = checkout_unit_names(APP_DIR)
    if DATA_PLANE_UNIT not in names:
        names = [*installed_unit_names(), DATA_PLANE_UNIT]
    return stop_order(names)


def egress(target: str | None) -> dict[str, str]:
    if not target:
        return {}
    out = run(["ip", "-4", "route", "get", target], timeout=10).stdout
    src = re.search(r"\bsrc ([0-9.]+)", out)
    dev = re.search(r"\bdev (\S+)", out)
    return {"src": src.group(1) if src else "", "dev": dev.group(1) if dev else ""}


def input_status() -> str:
    """`vpn-relay-apply input-status` — one line (off | OK … | PENDING CONFIRM … — why |
    ABSENT …), "" when it could not tell."""
    out = run([APPLY_HELPER, "input-status"], timeout=20)
    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in out.stdout.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    return lines[-1][:600] if out.returncode == 0 and lines else ""


def checkout_ref() -> dict[str, str]:
    head = run(["git", "-C", str(APP_DIR), "rev-parse", "HEAD"], timeout=15).stdout.strip()
    tag = run(["git", "-C", str(APP_DIR), "describe", "--tags", "--always"], timeout=15).stdout.strip()
    return {"commit": head, "describe": tag}


def facts(*, with_check: bool) -> dict[str, Any]:
    env = read_env()
    host = env_value(env, "RELAY_UPSTREAM_HOST")
    target = live_target()
    data: dict[str, Any] = {
        "agent": AGENT_VERSION,
        "protocol": PROTOCOL,
        "target_host": host or env_value(env, "RELAY_UPSTREAM_IPV4"),
        "tcp": ports_of(env_value(env, "RELAY_FORWARD_TCP_PORTS")),
        "udp": ports_of(env_value(env, "RELAY_FORWARD_UDP_PORTS")),
        "live_target": target,
        "resolved": resolve(host) if host else [],
        "ip_forward": run(["sysctl", "-n", "net.ipv4.ip_forward"], timeout=5).stdout.strip(),
        # The data plane and every timer of the set (a oneshot a timer runs is
        # "inactive" between its runs — its timer is what tells).
        "units": {unit: unit_state(unit) for unit in relay_units()
                  if unit == DATA_PLANE_UNIT or unit.endswith(".timer")},
        "ssh_ports": ssh_ports(),
        "egress": egress(target),
        "checkout": checkout_ref(),
        "update": read_json(UPDATE_FILE) or {},
        "input_status": input_status(),
    }
    jump = jump_state()
    if jump is not None:
        data["jump"] = jump
    if with_check:
        out = run([APPLY_HELPER, "check"], timeout=90)
        data["check"] = {
            "rc": out.returncode,
            "lines": [ln for ln in (out.stdout + out.stderr).splitlines() if ln.strip()][-25:],
        }
    return data


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Commands
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def pairing() -> dict[str, Any]:
    data = read_json(PAIRING_FILE)
    if data is None or not isinstance(data.get("token_sha256"), str):
        raise Denied("this relay has no pairing (run scripts/install.sh with a pairing code)")
    return data


def require_paired() -> dict[str, Any]:
    data = pairing()
    if not data.get("paired_at"):
        raise Denied("not paired yet: hello first")
    return data


def cmd_hello(args: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    token = args["token"]
    with exclusive():
        data = pairing()
        digest = hashlib.sha256(token.encode("ascii")).hexdigest()
        if not hmac.compare_digest(digest, str(data["token_sha256"])):
            raise Denied("token does not match this relay's pairing code")
        if not data.get("paired_at"):
            exp = data.get("exp")
            if not isinstance(exp, int) or time.time() > exp + HELLO_GRACE_SECONDS:
                raise Denied("the pairing code has expired — issue a new one in the bot and re-run the installer")
            data["paired_at"] = int(time.time())
            write_json(PAIRING_FILE, data)
        return {"paired_at": data["paired_at"], **facts(with_check=False)}


def cmd_status(_: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    require_paired()
    return facts(with_check=True)


def only_input_filter_failures(check_output: str) -> bool:
    """Every FAIL line of `vpn-relay-apply check` is about the input filter.

    check exits with the code of its FIRST failure and runs the input filter's steps
    before the forwarding, conntrack, TCP and TLS ones, so an exit 16-18 alone does not
    say the upstream answered — the FAIL lines do.
    """
    fails = [line for line in check_output.splitlines() if "FAIL: " in line]
    return bool(fails) and all("vpnrelay_input" in line or "listening but filtered" in line for line in fails)


def read_text_or_none(path: Path) -> str | None:
    try:
        return path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None


def restore_text(path: Path, text: str | None) -> None:
    if text is None:
        with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
            path.unlink()
    else:
        write_atomic(path, text, 0o644)


def cmd_apply(args: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    target = args["target"]
    if not valid_dns_name(target):
        raise Refused(f"target: {target!r} is not a DNS name")
    tcp, udp = parse_ports(args["tcp"]), parse_ports(args["udp"])
    with exclusive():
        require_paired()
        clash = sorted(set(tcp) & set(ssh_ports()))
        if clash:
            raise Refused(f"tcp {clash} is where sshd listens — forwarding it would lock the bot out")
        if not resolve(target):
            raise Failed(f"{target} does not resolve to an IPv4 address on the relay — nothing changed")
        before = read_env()
        # apply rewrites the last-known address for the NEW name; a rollback whose old
        # name does not resolve right now needs the old one back, or it is refused (20).
        cache_before = read_text_or_none(UPSTREAM_STATE)
        after = env_with(
            before,
            {
                "RELAY_UPSTREAM_IPV4": None,
                "RELAY_UPSTREAM_HOST": target,
                "RELAY_FORWARD_TCP_PORTS": ",".join(map(str, tcp)),
                "RELAY_FORWARD_UDP_PORTS": ",".join(map(str, udp)),
            },
        )
        write_atomic(ENV_FILE, after)
        applied = run([APPLY_HELPER, "apply"], timeout=120)
        checked = run([APPLY_HELPER, "check"], timeout=90) if applied.returncode == 0 else None
        # Only a passing check, or one whose every failure is the input filter's (16-18,
        # not what apply changed — judged by the FAIL lines, not the first exit code),
        # keeps the new forward. Everything else rolls back: 13/14 the upstream does not
        # answer, 10-12/15/20 the table or the sysctls did not take, 124 the check timed
        # out (never validated), 127 it could not run.
        kept = checked is not None and (
            checked.returncode == 0
            or (checked.returncode in (16, 17, 18) and only_input_filter_failures(checked.stdout + checked.stderr))
        )
        if applied.returncode != 0 or not kept:
            write_atomic(ENV_FILE, before)
            restore_text(UPSTREAM_STATE, cache_before)
            back = run([APPLY_HELPER, "apply"], timeout=120)
            failed = applied if applied.returncode != 0 or checked is None else checked
            restored = "restored" if back.returncode == 0 else f"RESTORE FAILED, rc {back.returncode}"
            raise Failed(
                f"the new forward did not work (vpn-relay-apply exit {failed.returncode}), rolled back "
                f"({restored}): {tail(failed.stdout + failed.stderr)}"
            )
        return {"applied": {"target": target, "tcp": tcp, "udp": udp}, **facts(with_check=False)}


def _transient(unit: str, internal: str, timeout: int) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    if SELFTEST:
        return run([AGENT_PATH, internal], timeout=timeout)
    return run(
        ["systemd-run", f"--unit={unit}", "--collect", "--wait", "--quiet",
         "-p", f"TimeoutStartSec={timeout}", AGENT_PATH, internal],
        timeout=timeout + 30,
    )


def cmd_update(_: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    with exclusive():
        require_paired()
        done = _transient("vpn-relay-update", "--internal-update", UPDATE_TIMEOUT)
    result = read_json(UPDATE_FILE) or {}
    if done.returncode != 0 or result.get("state") == "failed":
        if result.get("state") != "failed":
            # The unit ended without writing its verdict (killed, crashed): say so,
            # never the stale "running" line as if it were the cause.
            result = {**result, "state": "failed", "reason": "failed",
                      "message": f"the update unit ended without a result (exit {done.returncode}): "
                                 f"{tail(done.stderr, 3) or 'see journalctl -u vpn-relay-update'}"}
        raise Failed(str(result.get("message") or f"update unit exit {done.returncode}"), extra={"update": result})
    return {"update": result}


def cmd_uninstall(_: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    with exclusive():
        require_paired()
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            UNINSTALL_RESULT.unlink()
        done = _transient("vpn-relay-uninstall", "--internal-uninstall", 300)
    result = read_json(UNINSTALL_RESULT) or {}
    if done.returncode != 0 or not result.get("ok"):
        raise Failed(str(result.get("message") or tail(done.stderr) or f"uninstall unit exit {done.returncode}"))
    return {"uninstall": result}


def cmd_input_confirm(_: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    require_paired()
    # A direct child, never systemd-run: this ssh session must be among the helper's
    # ancestors — it is the proof. No agent lock (see the module docstring).
    done = run([APPLY_HELPER, "input-confirm"], timeout=60)
    lines = [ln for ln in (done.stdout + done.stderr).splitlines() if ln.strip()][-12:]
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Failed(f"vpn-relay-apply input-confirm exit {done.returncode}: {tail(done.stdout + done.stderr, 3)}")
    return {"input_confirm": {"rc": done.returncode, "lines": lines}, "input_status": input_status()}


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The jump line (a hub)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def authorized_keys_path() -> Path:
    """root's authorized_keys as install.sh found it (install.json), else the default."""
    value = (installer_relay() or {}).get("authorized_keys")
    return Path(_ROOT + value) if isinstance(value, str) and value.startswith("/") else P(DEFAULT_AUTHORIZED_KEYS)


def is_jump_line(line: str) -> bool:
    text = line.strip()
    return text.startswith(JUMP_PREFIX) and text.endswith(f" {JUMP_COMMENT}")


def jump_line(blob: str, opens: Sequence[tuple[str, int]]) -> str:
    permits = ",".join(f'permitopen="{host}:{port}"' for host, port in opens)
    return f"{JUMP_PREFIX}{permits},{JUMP_COMMAND} ssh-ed25519 {blob} {JUMP_COMMENT}"


def key_sha256(blob: str) -> str:
    """OpenSSH's fingerprint of a public key blob: SHA256:<base64, no padding>."""
    digest = hashlib.sha256(base64.b64decode(blob)).digest()
    return "SHA256:" + base64.b64encode(digest).decode().rstrip("=")


def jump_state() -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """The jump line as it is in the file: the relays it opens and its key's
    fingerprint; None without one."""
    try:
        text = authorized_keys_path().read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        return None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if is_jump_line(line):
            fields = line.split()
            opens = re.findall(r'permitopen="([^"]+)"', fields[0])
            blob = fields[2] if len(fields) >= 3 else ""
            try:
                fp = key_sha256(blob)
            except (ValueError, binascii.Error):
                fp = ""
            return {"open": opens, "key_sha256": fp}
    return None


def write_jump_line(path: Path, line: str | None, blob: str | None) -> bool:
    """Put *line* (None: no line) where the jump line is, every other line byte-
    identical. True when the file changed."""
    try:
        original = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        if line is None:
            return False
        raise Failed(f"{path} does not exist — not a relay this agent was installed on") from None
    lines = original.splitlines(keepends=True)
    if blob is not None and any(blob in old and not is_jump_line(old) for old in lines):
        raise Refused("this key already has another line in authorized_keys — refusing to make it a jump key")
    kept: list[str] = []
    placed = line is None
    for old in lines:
        if not is_jump_line(old):
            kept.append(old)
        elif not placed:
            kept.append(f"{line}\n" if old.endswith("\n") else str(line))
            placed = True
    if not placed:
        if kept and not kept[-1].endswith("\n"):
            kept[-1] += "\n"
        kept.append(f"{line}\n")
    text = "".join(kept)
    if text == original:
        return False
    st = path.stat()
    write_atomic(path, text, st.st_mode & 0o777)
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.chown(path, st.st_uid, st.st_gid)
    return True


def sshd_forwarding() -> dict[str, str]:
    """The effective forwarding settings of this sshd (`sshd -T`), Failed when it cannot tell."""
    out = run(["sshd", "-T"], timeout=20)
    if out.returncode != 0:
        raise Failed(f"sshd -T failed (exit {out.returncode}): {tail(out.stderr or out.stdout, 2)}")
    found: dict[str, str] = {}
    for line in out.stdout.splitlines():
        key, _, value = line.strip().partition(" ")
        if key in ("allowtcpforwarding", "allowstreamlocalforwarding", "disableforwarding"):
            found[key] = value.strip().lower()
    return found


def require_local_forwarding() -> None:
    """A jump line only where sshd forwards local TCP and nothing else (see the docstring)."""
    found = sshd_forwarding()
    tcp = found.get("allowtcpforwarding", "?")
    unix = found.get("allowstreamlocalforwarding", "?")
    if found.get("disableforwarding") == "yes" or tcp == "no":
        raise Failed(f"sshd forwards nothing here (allowtcpforwarding {tcp}, disableforwarding "
                     f"{found.get('disableforwarding', '?')}) — the jump would not work")
    if tcp != "local" or unix != "no":
        raise Failed(f"sshd forwards more than local TCP here (allowtcpforwarding {tcp}, allowstreamlocalforwarding "
                     f"{unix}): a jump key could open listeners on this host — deploy this relay first "
                     "(scripts/deploy.sh installs /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-vpnrelay-forwarding.conf)")


def cmd_jump(args: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    blob = ed25519_blob(args["key"])
    opens = parse_opens(args["open"])
    require_paired()
    require_local_forwarding()
    with exclusive(JUMP_LOCK_FILE):
        path = authorized_keys_path()
        changed = write_jump_line(path, jump_line(blob, opens), blob)
    return {"jump": {"open": [f"{host}:{port}" for host, port in opens], "key_sha256": key_sha256(blob),
                     "changed": changed}}


def cmd_jump_off(_: dict[str, str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    require_paired()
    with exclusive(JUMP_LOCK_FILE):
        changed = write_jump_line(authorized_keys_path(), None, None)
    return {"jump": {"open": [], "changed": changed}}


COMMANDS = {
    "hello": cmd_hello,
    "status": cmd_status,
    "apply": cmd_apply,
    "update": cmd_update,
    "uninstall": cmd_uninstall,
    "input-confirm": cmd_input_confirm,
    "jump": cmd_jump,
    "jump-off": cmd_jump_off,
}


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Internal: update (in its own transient unit)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def _release_key(tag: str) -> tuple[int, ...]:
    return tuple(int(x) for x in tag[1:].split("."))


def latest_release(listing: str) -> str | None:
    """The newest release tag of a `git tag -l --sort=refname v*` listing, or None.

    One name per line (split on "\\n" only, as bash's `read` splits); a release is a
    full RELEASE_TAG_RE match, compared by _release_key; of equal keys the first wins
    (max). scripts/deploy.sh's relay_latest_release is the same rule.
    """
    tags = [t for t in listing.split("\n") if RELEASE_TAG_RE.fullmatch(t)]
    return max(tags, key=_release_key) if tags else None


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# DEPLOY VERDICT — one rule, carried VERBATIM by scripts/vpn-relay-agent (`update`)
# and scripts/wizard/vpn-bot-wizard-update (the main server's «Обновить бота»);
# tests/test_deploy_verdict.py pins the two blocks byte-identical, the reasons
# against deploy.sh's DEPLOY_FAIL_REASONS and the bot's i18n.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# deploy.sh's reason=<class> (its DEPLOY_FAIL_REASONS), plus the waiter's own:
# "timeout" — the deploy did not finish while the caller waited for it.
DEPLOY_REASONS = (
    "busy", "fetch", "preflight", "no_venv", "tests", "checks", "upstream", "rolled_back", "failed", "timeout",
)
_DV_RESULT = re.compile(
    r"\[deploy:result (?:ok|noop|failed step=(?P<step>[a-z_]{1,32}) reason=(?P<reason>[a-z_]{1,32}))\]"
)
_DV_WARN = re.compile(r"^\[deploy:warn (?P<code>[a-z_]{1,48})\] ?(?P<text>.*)$", re.MULTILINE)
_DV_LOG = re.compile(r"^redeploy: launching \S+ \(log: (?P<log>/\S+)\)$", re.MULTILINE)
_DV_PYTEST_SUMMARY = re.compile(r"^=+ .*\b[0-9]+ (?:failed|errors?)\b.* in [0-9.]+s.*=+$")
_DV_PYTEST_NODE = re.compile(r"^(?:FAILED|ERROR) tests/")
DV_EXCERPT_LINES = 8
DV_EXCERPT_CHARS = 300


def _dv_guess(lines: list[str], rc: int) -> str:
    """The reason of a deploy.sh that printed no result line (one that predates the
    markers), read from its text the way an operator reads it."""
    text = "\n".join(lines)
    if rc == 124:
        return "timeout"
    if "another deploy already holds" in text:
        return "busy"
    if "ensurepip is not available" in text or re.search(r"\bpython3\.[0-9]+-venv\b", text):
        return "no_venv"
    if "===== ROLLBACK REPORT" in text:
        if re.search(r"vpn-relay-apply check failed after the restart \(exit 1[34]\b", text):
            return "upstream"
        return "rolled_back"
    if any(_DV_PYTEST_SUMMARY.match(ln) or _DV_PYTEST_NODE.match(ln) for ln in lines):
        return "tests"
    fails = [ln for ln in lines if "[deploy][FAIL] " in ln]
    if fails:
        return "fetch" if "git fetch" in fails[-1] else "checks"
    return "failed"


def _dv_excerpt(lines: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """The lines an operator looks at first: the rollback's reason, deploy.sh's FAIL
    lines, the relay check's FAIL lines, the failed tests and pytest's summary, the
    ensurepip hint — the last DV_EXCERPT_LINES of them, each capped."""
    picked: list[str] = []
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        rollback_reason = (
            "[deploy][WARN] " in line and i + 1 < len(lines) and "[deploy][WARN] ROLLBACK" in lines[i + 1]
        )
        if (
            rollback_reason
            or "[deploy][FAIL] " in line
            or "FAIL: " in line
            or _DV_PYTEST_NODE.match(line)
            or _DV_PYTEST_SUMMARY.match(line)
            or "ensurepip is not available" in line
            or re.search(r"\bapt install python3\.[0-9]+-venv\b", line)
        ):
            text = line.strip()[:DV_EXCERPT_CHARS]
            if text not in picked:
                picked.append(text)
    return picked[-DV_EXCERPT_LINES:]


def deploy_verdict(output: str, rc: int) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Why a deploy (redeploy.sh -> deploy.sh) ended as it did, for the bot.

    ``{"reason", "step", "excerpt", "warnings", "log"}``: reason is one of
    DEPLOY_REASONS, or "" when the deploy did not fail (ok, noop); step is deploy.sh's
    step it failed in ("" when unknown); excerpt the significant lines; warnings the
    ``[deploy:warn]`` findings of a deploy that succeeded ({"code", "text"}); log the
    deploy log redeploy.sh named. deploy.sh's own result line decides when there is
    one; without it the text does (a deploy.sh that predates the markers).
    """
    lines = [ln.rstrip() for ln in output.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    found = None
    for match in _DV_RESULT.finditer(output):
        found = match
    reason = step = ""
    if rc == 124:
        reason = "timeout"
    elif found is not None:
        if found.group("reason") is not None:
            reason = found.group("reason") if found.group("reason") in DEPLOY_REASONS else "failed"
            step = found.group("step") or ""
        elif rc != 0:
            reason = "failed"
    elif rc != 0:
        reason = _dv_guess(lines, rc)
    if not step:
        steps = re.findall(r"\[deploy:step [0-9]+/[0-9]+ ([a-z_]{1,32})\]", output)
        step = steps[-1] if reason and steps else ""
    log = _DV_LOG.search(output)
    return {
        "reason": reason,
        "step": step,
        "excerpt": _dv_excerpt(lines) if reason else [],
        "warnings": [
            {"code": m.group("code"), "text": m.group("text").strip()[:DV_EXCERPT_CHARS]}
            for m in _DV_WARN.finditer(output)
        ],
        "log": log.group("log") if log else "",
    }
# --- DEPLOY VERDICT (end) ---


def _deploy_reason(output: str) -> str:
    """Why deploy.sh ended as it did, in its own words (one line, capped).

    A rollback: the WARN right before "ROLLBACK (relay):" (rollback_now's reason). A
    stop before Phase 2: the last FAIL line. A no-op: its "nothing to deploy" line.
    """
    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in output.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    warn, fail, info = "[deploy][WARN] ", "[deploy][FAIL] ", "[deploy] "
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        if f"{warn}ROLLBACK (relay):" in line and i and warn in lines[i - 1]:
            return lines[i - 1].split(warn, 1)[1][:600]
    fails = [ln.split(fail, 1)[1] for ln in lines if fail in ln]
    if fails:
        return fails[-1][:600]
    noops = [ln.split(info, 1)[1] for ln in lines if info in ln and "nothing to deploy" in ln]
    if noops:
        return noops[-1][:600]
    return tail(output, 3)[:600]


def internal_update() -> int:
    started = int(time.time())

    def note(state: str, message: str, **extra: Any) -> None:
        write_json(UPDATE_FILE, {"state": state, "message": message, "started_at": started,
                                 "finished_at": int(time.time()) if state != "running" else None, **extra}, 0o644)

    if installer_relay() is None:
        note("failed", "this is not a relay installed by install.sh — refusing", reason="preflight")
        return 1
    note("running", "fetching release tags")
    git = ["git", "-C", str(APP_DIR)]
    old = run([*git, "rev-parse", "HEAD"], timeout=15).stdout.strip()
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", old):
        note("failed", f"{APP_DIR} is not a git checkout", reason="preflight")
        return 1
    fetched = run([*git, "fetch", "--quiet", "--tags", "--force", "origin"], timeout=180)
    if fetched.returncode != 0:
        note("failed", f"git fetch failed: {tail(fetched.stderr)}", from_commit=old, reason="fetch",
             excerpt=tail(fetched.stderr, 4).splitlines())
        return 1
    latest = latest_release(run([*git, *TAG_LIST], timeout=15).stdout)
    if latest is None:
        note("noop", "no release tag (v*) in the repository", from_commit=old)
        return 0
    target = run([*git, "rev-parse", f"{latest}^{{commit}}"], timeout=15).stdout.strip()
    if target == old or run([*git, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", target, old], timeout=15).returncode == 0:
        note("noop", f"already at or past {latest}", from_commit=old, release=latest)
        return 0
    if run([*git, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", old, target], timeout=15).returncode != 0:
        note("failed", f"{old[:12]} is not an ancestor of {latest} — not moving sideways", from_commit=old,
             release=latest, reason="preflight")
        return 1
    redeploy = APP_DIR / REDEPLOY
    try:
        knows_ref = "DEPLOY_REF" in redeploy.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        knows_ref = False
    if not knows_ref:
        note("failed", f"{redeploy} of this checkout cannot deploy a release (no DEPLOY_REF) — "
             "deploy the relay once by hand: sudo DEPLOY_REF=main bash scripts/redeploy.sh",
             from_commit=old, release=latest, reason="preflight")
        return 1
    note("running", f"deploying {latest} (scripts/redeploy.sh, DEPLOY_REF={latest})", from_commit=old, release=latest)
    # The deploy an operator runs, unattended: redeploy.sh starts the tag's deploy.sh
    # in its own transient unit and, with REDEPLOY_ATTACH=pipe, waits and exits with
    # deploy.sh's code. deploy.sh re-checks forward-only itself and rolls back by itself.
    done = run(["bash", str(redeploy)], env={"DEPLOY_REF": latest, "REDEPLOY_ATTACH": "pipe"},
               timeout=UPDATE_TIMEOUT - 120)
    output = done.stdout + done.stderr
    verdict_of = deploy_verdict(output, done.returncode)
    where = {"log": verdict_of["log"]} if verdict_of["log"] else {}
    if verdict_of["warnings"]:
        where["warnings"] = verdict_of["warnings"]
    now = run([*git, "rev-parse", "HEAD"], timeout=15).stdout.strip()
    if done.returncode == 0 and now == target:
        note("succeeded", f"updated to {latest}", from_commit=old, to_commit=target, release=latest, **where)
        return 0
    if done.returncode == 0 and now == old:
        note("noop", f"deploy.sh found nothing to deploy for {latest}: {_deploy_reason(output)}",
             from_commit=old, release=latest, **where)
        return 0
    if done.returncode == 124:
        verdict = f"did not finish within {UPDATE_TIMEOUT - 120}s (it may still run: systemctl status vpn-bot-deploy)"
    elif ROLLBACK_REPORT in output:
        verdict = f"failed and rolled back (exit {done.returncode})"
    elif DEPLOY_OK in output:
        verdict = f"reported DEPLOY OK but the checkout is at {now[:12] or '?'}, not {target[:12]}"
    else:
        verdict = f"stopped before any change (exit {done.returncode})"
    note("failed", f"the deploy of {latest} {verdict}: {_deploy_reason(output)}",
         from_commit=old, release=latest, **({"now_commit": now} if now != old else {}), **where,
         reason=verdict_of["reason"] or "failed", step=verdict_of["step"],
         excerpt=verdict_of["excerpt"] or tail(output, 4).splitlines())
    return 1


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Internal: uninstall (in its own transient unit)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def strip_agent_keys(path: Path) -> int:
    """Drop every authorized_keys line that runs this agent, and the jump line; the
    rest stays byte-identical."""
    try:
        original = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return 0
    lines = original.splitlines(keepends=True)
    kept = [line for line in lines if KEY_MARKER not in line and not is_jump_line(line)]
    if len(kept) != len(lines):
        st = path.stat()
        write_atomic(path, "".join(kept), st.st_mode & 0o777)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.chown(path, st.st_uid, st.st_gid)
    return len(lines) - len(kept)


def installer_relay() -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """install.json when this host is a relay scripts/install.sh installed, else None."""
    install = read_json(INSTALL_FILE)
    if install is None or install.get("installer") != "vpn-relay":
        return None
    env = ENV_FILE.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if ENV_FILE.exists() else ""
    if (UNIT_DIR / "vpn-bot.service").exists() or env_value(env, "NODE_ROLE") != "relay":
        return None
    return install


def table_gone(family: str, table: str) -> bool:
    """Proven absent: nft ran and said so (a timeout or a missing nft proves nothing)."""
    return run(["nft", "list", "table", family, table], timeout=10).returncode not in (0, 124, 127)


def internal_uninstall() -> int:
    steps: list[str] = []
    install = installer_relay()
    if install is None:
        write_json(UNINSTALL_RESULT, {"ok": False, "message": "this is not a relay installed by install.sh — refusing"})
        return 1
    # Read once, before anything is removed (the checkout may go at the end): timers,
    # then the oneshots, vpn-relay.service last (its ExecStop removes the tables).
    units = relay_units()
    for unit in units:
        run(["systemctl", "disable", "--now", unit], timeout=60)
    run(["systemctl", "stop", "vpn-relay-input-deadman.timer"], timeout=30)
    for family, table in TABLES:
        if run(["nft", "list", "table", family, table], timeout=10).returncode == 0:
            run(["nft", "delete", "table", family, table], timeout=10)
    # Nothing that a retry needs (the key, the pairing, the helpers) goes before the
    # data plane is really gone: a table that survived would keep forwarding with no
    # way left for the bot to finish the job.
    left = [f"{family} {table}" for family, table in TABLES if not table_gone(family, table)]
    if left:
        message = (f"table {', '.join(left)} could not be removed — the units are stopped, but the key, "
                   "the pairing and the helpers stay so the bot can retry uninstall")
        write_json(UNINSTALL_RESULT, {"ok": False, "message": message, "steps": steps})
        journal(message)
        return 1
    steps.append(f"units stopped and disabled ({', '.join(units)}), tables removed")
    for unit in units:
        with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
            (UNIT_DIR / unit).unlink()
    run(["systemctl", "daemon-reload"], timeout=60)
    with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
        SYSCTL_FILE.unlink()
    before = str(install.get("ip_forward_before", "0"))
    run(["sysctl", "-q", "-w", f"net.ipv4.ip_forward={'1' if before == '1' else '0'}"], timeout=10)
    steps.append(f"sysctl file removed, ip_forward={before}")
    keys = authorized_keys_path()
    steps.append(f"{strip_agent_keys(keys)} agent/jump key line(s) removed from {keys}")
    for path in (P(APPLY_HELPER), STATE_DIR, VAR_DIR):
        if path.is_dir():
            shutil.rmtree(path, ignore_errors=True)
        else:
            with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
                path.unlink()
    if install.get("created_app_dir") is True and APP_DIR.is_dir():
        shutil.rmtree(APP_DIR, ignore_errors=True)
        steps.append(f"{APP_DIR} removed")
    backups = install.get("adoption_backup")
    message = "relay uninstalled" + (f"; the pre-install relay is kept in {backups}" if backups else "")
    with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
        P(AGENT_PATH).unlink()
    write_json(UNINSTALL_RESULT, {"ok": True, "message": message, "steps": steps})
    journal(message)
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Entry
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def emit(payload: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    sys.stdout.flush()


def main(argv: Sequence[str]) -> int:
    if len(argv) == 2 and argv[1] in ("--internal-update", "--internal-uninstall"):
        if "SSH_CONNECTION" in os.environ or (os.geteuid() != 0 and not SELFTEST):
            sys.stderr.write("vpn-relay-agent: internal entry points run only as root, outside ssh\n")
            return E_REFUSED
        return internal_update() if argv[1] == "--internal-update" else internal_uninstall()
    if len(argv) != 1:
        emit({"ok": False, "error": "arguments are not accepted; the request comes from SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND"})
        return E_REFUSED
    caller = (os.environ.get("SSH_CONNECTION") or "local").split(" ")[0]
    name = "?"
    try:
        name, args = parse_request(os.environ.get("SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND"))
        payload = COMMANDS[name](args)
    except Refused as exc:
        rc, payload = E_REFUSED, {"ok": False, "error": f"refused: {exc}"}
    except Denied as exc:
        rc, payload = E_DENIED, {"ok": False, "error": str(exc)}
    except Busy as exc:
        rc, payload = E_BUSY, {"ok": False, "error": str(exc)}
    except Failed as exc:
        rc, payload = E_FAILED, {**exc.extra, "ok": False, "error": str(exc)}
    except Exception as exc:  # the bot gets a reason, never a traceback
        rc, payload = E_FAILED, {"ok": False, "error": f"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}"}
    else:
        rc, payload = E_OK, {"ok": True, **payload}
    payload["cmd"] = name
    journal(f"{name} from {caller}: {'ok' if rc == 0 else 'rc ' + str(rc)}")
    emit(payload)
    return rc


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
